0..75 Comment "// Transport along a path between types built from an equivalence, the HoTT"
76..151 Comment "// book\'s § 2.10 (`ua`) and Lemma 2.10.5 (transport along `ua(e)` is `e`),"
152..227 Comment "// in the family of lists: negation, its own inverse, makes a path from the"
228..303 Comment "// booleans to themselves, and transport along it negates every element, by"
304..380 Comment "// conversion and by a run. A pair of maps whose round trips differ makes no"
381..456 Comment "// path. Between types of lists, `equiv` covers one cell over a rigid tail:"
457..527 Comment "// the empty list, then one cell per element pattern, the tail a fresh"
528..577 Comment "// variable a round trip returns without reading."
578..580 Comment "//"
581..616 Comment "// - see: #1480 — `flipped_value`"
617..669 Comment "// - see: #1064 — `moved_inline`, `flipped_inline`"
671..716 Comment "// Negation and the identity on the booleans."
